{
  "summary": "Caps relative ban durations to uint32_t across the setban RPC and the -bantime startup option. setban rejects relative ban times exceeding UINT32_MAX with an RPC error, and -bantime parses the argument as uint32_t, saturating larger values at UINT32_MAX. Absolute ban timestamps remain unaffected.",
  "problem": "BanMan calculates ban expiration as GetTime() + bantime using signed 64-bit integers. A relative bantime near INT64_MAX triggers signed integer overflow; on standard builds the sum wraps negative, causing the node to treat the ban as already expired and silently drop it while the RPC still reports success.",
  "evidence": [
    "UBSan runtime error cited in the description: 'src/banman.cpp:140:73: runtime error: signed integer overflow: 1790412558 + 9223372036854775807 cannot be represented in type int64_t'"
  ],
