  "changed_since_previous": "Switched from checking whether GetTime() + banTime overflows int64_t to enforcing a fixed limit of UINT32_MAX on relative durations in setban, and added uint32_t saturation handling for the -bantime configuration argument in init.cpp.",
  "card": "Caps relative ban durations to UINT32_MAX across the setban RPC and the -bantime startup parameter. Passing relative ban durations near INT64_MAX currently overflows signed 64-bit addition in BanMan, causing UB under UBSan and wrapping to a negative timestamp that silently drops the ban while setban reports success. With this change, setban throws an invalid parameter error for relative durations above UINT32_MAX, and -bantime saturates at UINT32_MAX.",
